/* Hero showcase, tab 3 "Click to edit".

   The site workspace of the Tracy app: the left rail, the chat with the
   site's start card, and the site in the app's own browser. The pointer
   comes in from the bottom-right edge, turns on Edit, glides over a few
   blocks of the page (each gets the app's orange line), picks the big
   headline, types a short request in the comment box and clicks "Ask Tracy
   to edit". Tracy then answers in the chat and the headline on the page
   changes. Last (D-32), the pointer clicks Undo on the "Changed on the site"
   card, confirms inside the card, and the page goes back to the old headline.

   Copied from the live app (cowork.tracy.site, test site kinetic-demo, read
   23/10/2026, window 1280 x 696): sizes and colours with getComputedStyle,
   icons from the page's own SVG (and from the app's script for the start
   card icons, which were no longer on screen), every chat line word for word
   and in the app's order. One real request was sent once to record the run:
   the app took 23s from the click to the answer; here the same steps run in
   7s. The undo was also pressed once for real: 1.6s from the confirm to
   "Undone", then the preview reloads (its loading line) with the old page.
   The page is two screenshots of the test site at the app's frame size
   (699.5 x 603): as it was, and after Tracy's edit. Account data is made up;
   addresses use .tracy.ai (D-07). */
